From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: map the user shared data a whole host page at a time.

With the environment reaching Wine, it finds its prefix, decides the prefix
needs wineboot, and stops there:

    err:virtual:virtual_init_user_shared_data failed to remap the process USD: 0

res is 0, so server_get_unix_fd worked and it is the mmap that failed -- which
the message could not say, because it only ever prints res.

The length is the likely reason: it asks for sizeof(KUSER_SHARED_DATA), and this
console's pages are 16 KiB, so that is not a whole page. The section is exactly
one host page wide (patch 0102), so map it that way. virtual_map_user_shared_data
already passes a page-sized length and is reached first, without complaint.

Both messages now print errno as well, so if the length was not the reason the
next run says what was.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5130,7 +5130,11 @@ void virtual_map_user_shared_data(void)
     if ((res = server_get_unix_fd( section, 0, &fd, &needs_close, NULL, NULL )) ||
         (user_shared_data != mmap( user_shared_data, page_size, PROT_READ, MAP_SHARED|MAP_FIXED, fd, 0 )))
     {
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+        ERR( "failed to remap the process USD: %d errno %d\n", res, errno );
+#else
         ERR( "failed to remap the process USD: %d\n", res );
+#endif
         exit(1);
     }
     if (needs_close) close( fd );
@@ -5158,12 +5162,27 @@ void virtual_init_user_shared_data(void)
         ERR( "failed to open the USD section: %08x\n", status );
         exit(1);
     }
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ Map a whole host page. This console's pages are 16 KiB, and the
+     * section is exactly one of them (patch 0102); mmap refuses a length that
+     * is not a multiple of a page. The error below prints errno too, because
+     * res is 0 whenever it is the mmap rather than the fd that failed. */
+    if ((res = server_get_unix_fd( section, 0, &fd, &needs_close, NULL, NULL )) ||
+        (data = mmap( NULL, (sizeof(*data) + host_page_size - 1) & ~(host_page_size - 1),
+                      PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED, fd, 0 )) == MAP_FAILED)
+    {
+        ERR( "failed to remap the process USD: %d errno %d size %u host_page %u\n",
+             res, errno, (unsigned int)sizeof(*data), (unsigned int)host_page_size );
+        exit(1);
+    }
+#else
     if ((res = server_get_unix_fd( section, 0, &fd, &needs_close, NULL, NULL )) ||
         (data = mmap( NULL, sizeof(*data), PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED, fd, 0 )) == MAP_FAILED)
     {
         ERR( "failed to remap the process USD: %d\n", res );
         exit(1);
     }
+#endif
     if (needs_close) close( fd );
     NtClose( section );
 
